Now ask a question you can answer by counting. *If the price were \$12, how many of these people would buy?*

Everyone whose maximum is \$12 or more. Scan the column: R1, R3, R6, R7, R9, R10. Six people, so six meals.

Do that at every price anyone named and you have a demand curve. The mechanical version is to sort by willingness to pay from high to low and keep a running count.


